{:edb/db-before-t 1572 :edb/db-after-t 1573 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534885 50 #inst "2026-10-08T10:06:29.121Z" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124316 1100 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1$?" 13194139534885 false] [17592186124316 1100 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1?$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124316 1145 "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1, \\qquad z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k \\in \\mathbb{R}$ can vary arbitrarily.\n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2: \\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2: \\dfrac{x^2}{3^2} + \\dfrac{(y+1)^2}{1^2} = 1\\right\\}\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(0,-1)$ with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $1$." 13194139534885 false] [17592186124316 1145 "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1, \\qquad z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k \\in \\mathbb{R}$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\dfrac{x^2}{9} + (y+1)^2 = 1\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left\\{ (x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\dfrac{x^2}{3^2} + \\dfrac{(y+1)^2}{1^2} = 1\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(0,-1)$ with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $1.$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124317 1100 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac {x^2} 2 +  \\dfrac {(y-2)^2}4  = 1?$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124317 1100 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac {x^2} 2 + \\dfrac {(y-2)^2}4 = 1$?" 13194139534885 false] [17592186124317 1145 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{0^{2}}{2} + ((y - 2)^{2})/(4) &= 1 \\\\\n(y - 2)^{2} &= 4 \\\\\ny - 2 &= ± 2 \\\\\ny &= 2 ± 2 \\\\\ny &= 0, 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=0$ and $y=4$ in the $yz$-plane." 13194139534885 false] [17592186124317 1145 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=0$ and $y=4$ in the $yz$-plane." 13194139534885 true] [17592186124508 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317419 13194139534885 true] [17592186124508 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317426 13194139534885 true] [17592186124508 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317433 13194139534885 true] [17592186124509 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317391 13194139534885 true] [17592186124509 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317398 13194139534885 true] [17592186124509 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317405 13194139534885 true] [17592186124509 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317412 13194139534885 true] [17592186124746 1017 #edb/ref 17592186121495 13194139534885 false] [17592186124746 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317385 13194139534885 true] [17592186124746 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534885 true] [17592186124746 1100 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $((x + 1)^{2})/(4) - ((y - 4)^{2})/(2) = 1$?" 13194139534885 false] [17592186124746 1100 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1?$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124746 1145 "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(-1,4).$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124795 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534885 true] [17592186124795 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic cylinder $9x^{2} + 2(y - 1)^{2} = 18$ and the plane $z = 1$ onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?" 13194139534885 false] [17592186124795 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic cylinder $9{x}^{2}+2(y-1)^{2}=18$ and the plane $z=1$ onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124795 1145 "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=1,$ we substitute $z=1$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+2(y-1)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(3)^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{2}$ and $3.$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124808 1017 #edb/ref 17592186121870 13194139534885 false] [17592186124808 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317440 13194139534885 true] [17592186124808 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534885 true] [17592186124808 1100 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $((x - 1)^{2})/(16) + ((y + 2)^{2})/(8) = 1$?" 13194139534885 false] [17592186124808 1100 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1?$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186124808 1145 "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(1,-2)$ with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317386 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317387 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317388 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317389 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317390 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1041 "selection" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317387 13194139534885 true] [17592186317385 1110 #uuid "d876644b-b2b3-5432-a6fb-95c01085e552" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317386 1034 "{R}^{2}" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534885 true] [17592186317386 1111 #uuid "fa94cf79-04ea-5119-b7b2-32d4c3a82a0a" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317387 1034 "A hyperbola centered at $(-1,4)$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317387 1111 #uuid "398108f0-8006-5cae-8c65-de61fbda6985" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317388 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }x\\ge 0}" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534885 true] [17592186317388 1111 #uuid "f5530ecb-279e-5ecb-a53e-23aa9c0a3d68" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317389 1034 "A hyperbola centered at $(1,-4)$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317389 1111 #uuid "20538cc1-0f0d-5b32-aaaf-73462763337d" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317390 1034 "A parabola centered at $(1,-4)$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317390 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317390 1111 #uuid "bd68a2a8-a3f0-5455-b025-7070a3c16cf0" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317391 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317392 13194139534885 true] [17592186317391 1089 "q-164398" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317391 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534885 true] [17592186317391 1100 "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1?$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317391 1113 #uuid "3402cf6a-d8e4-5082-a8db-072c1ad24c36" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317391 1145 "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =3\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =1,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $x=1$ and $x=5$ in the $xy$-plane." 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317393 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317394 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317395 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317396 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317397 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1041 "selection" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317395 13194139534885 true] [17592186317392 1110 #uuid "31747716-6593-5f8a-8b90-395a6a655b06" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317393 1034 "The hyperbola $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317393 1111 #uuid "723c343c-0f47-51d8-bb35-a3619d08f927" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317394 1034 "The line $x=5$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317394 1111 #uuid "6826f8e0-8569-5f32-b740-21b9fdd97887" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317395 1034 "The lines $x=1$ and $x=5$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317395 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317395 1111 #uuid "82963d38-17d9-5f5d-a422-6a77747d67c6" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317396 1034 "The ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317396 1111 #uuid "89640ad3-319c-5b7c-9cbb-3d9cc87141f4" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317397 1034 "The line $x=3$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317397 1111 #uuid "3348313e-e93b-53fe-950a-778491fc9c92" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317398 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317399 13194139534885 true] [17592186317398 1089 "q-164400" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317398 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534885 true] [17592186317398 1100 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x+3)^{2}=6y?$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317398 1113 #uuid "7c06a8e8-6e3d-50f3-ae2e-200f38471a76" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317398 1145 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+3)^{2} & =6y \\\\ 9 & =6y \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{6} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a line in the $yz$-plane." 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317400 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317401 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317402 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317403 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317404 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1041 "selection" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317403 13194139534885 true] [17592186317399 1110 #uuid "84a4f3de-bd74-5c02-a46d-c1fe74093a3a" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317400 1034 "The parabola $(x+3)^{2}=6z$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317400 1111 #uuid "d3c1db30-d60a-53f3-b2a2-cdbb3c4e4898" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317401 1034 "The line $y=3$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317401 1111 #uuid "b538c52f-58f4-525c-90b0-595d1bce9948" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317402 1034 "The parabola ${x}^{2}=6(z-3)$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317402 1111 #uuid "8a033994-7206-5d38-87a5-81db2249f53f" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317403 1034 "The line $y=\\frac{3}{2}$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317403 1111 #uuid "af9dd4a1-d1b8-5217-b51b-6f766f3b34c9" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317404 1034 "The lines $y=-3$ and $y=15$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317404 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317404 1111 #uuid "ec1267fb-48d3-5536-8811-3e6dd8eb8aa7" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317405 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317406 13194139534885 true] [17592186317405 1089 "q-164411" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317405 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534885 true] [17592186317405 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2}=12$ and the plane $y=1$ onto the $xz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317405 1113 #uuid "25bdc329-60cf-56f4-84fa-3414d97450cd" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317405 1145 "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $y=1,$ we substitute $y=1$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $y$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317407 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317408 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317409 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317410 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317411 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1041 "selection" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317409 13194139534885 true] [17592186317406 1110 #uuid "2b90d15e-01af-5ee6-9eb1-1df6cf3b7bc0" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317407 1034 "$4$ and $1$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317407 1111 #uuid "581a880f-0bee-593e-a0fe-021b2f89e73b" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317408 1034 "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317408 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317408 1111 #uuid "efd4100e-a77a-5b6d-8659-6d531d4fe79d" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317409 1034 "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317409 1111 #uuid "ba0aeada-f80b-5eac-a5c3-44173949397a" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317410 1034 "$4$ and $2$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317410 1111 #uuid "9771d26b-18a5-57ec-ab5c-803911edb87a" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317411 1034 "$2$ and $1$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317411 1111 #uuid "172fd8c6-f2e5-5640-88ed-61a271db7548" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317412 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317413 13194139534885 true] [17592186317412 1089 "q-164415" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317412 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534885 true] [17592186317412 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2}=10$ and the plane $z=5$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317412 1113 #uuid "6fceebe4-a56d-5581-86c4-4cef01c078e2" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317412 1145 "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=5,$ we substitute $z=5$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317414 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317415 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317416 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317417 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317418 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1041 "selection" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317416 13194139534885 true] [17592186317413 1110 #uuid "41d16978-9a2d-561d-933e-9c51c4124ec6" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317414 1034 "$5$ and $2$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317414 1111 #uuid "4dc6833a-3109-5cc5-955c-4b43c0b4fea8" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317415 1034 "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317415 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534885 true] [17592186317415 1111 #uuid "170e12cf-bb71-5428-a64b-fbac5bb0e3f1" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317416 1034 "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534885 true] [17592186317416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454